        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right foot lump symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Lump on the dorsum of the right foot near the base of the 4th toe is still present and somewhat annoying in enclosed shoes, especially cheap flats."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right foot lesion symptom history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild tenderness only when a shoe rubs the lesion; no pain at rest, itch, discharge, ulceration, or noticed colour change. Onset unclear; noticed this term, possibly last term. Subjectively stable in size, possibly slightly increased, but patient is unsure."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right dorsal foot lesion on examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 6–7 mm, firm, well-circumscribed, slightly raised dermal papule with tan-brown colour and smooth surface, on the dorsum of the right foot at the base of the 4th toe. Dimple sign present on lateral compression."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
